@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title The unit baseline — green means no new failing test
' purpose: how a branch proves it broke nothing while the unit suite is already red on the host it is built on
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/baseline.go
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/baseline_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/unit-baseline.txt
' covers: mise.toml
'   the decision ............ _spec/_plans/tui-responsiveness.puml (D12)
'   the gate it stands in ... _spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml (the standing gate)
'   the full gate ........... _spec/_devops/release-gate.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHY THIS EXISTS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' MEASURED 2026-11-10 at 0f34a714 (= main), darwin/arm64, with and without
' -race: `go test -count=1 ./...` fails 15 tests in 3 of 47 packages. None
' sits in a TUI package. Two fail on any host: envreg.go:153 puts
' PROVEO_GITHUB_TRANSPORT in the wrong block, and probe_test.go:30 names a
' `:latest` tag outside imagetest.Resolve. Thirteen trace to this macOS host:
' /bin/bash is 3.2, `flock` is absent, and a unix socket path under the test
' temp dir exceeds 104 bytes. The release gate runs `go test ./...` in its
' in-sandbox Linux half, where those thirteen are expected to pass.
' [Unverified] That they pass on Linux: no Linux run exists yet.
' `mise run ci` therefore exits non-zero on this host before any change, and
' a red suite cannot say whether a slice broke something.
' The Executor, 2026-11-10: "Since the failures are not TUI related, let Green
' be 'no new failing tests'".
'
' ── WHAT THE GATE DOES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' `mise run baseline` runs `go run ./cmd/proveo-dev baseline`: one
' `go test -race -count=1 -json ./...`, read as a stream.
'   a failing top-level test is "package Test", the module prefix trimmed
'   a subtest's failure belongs to its parent and is not listed twice
'   a package that fails with NO failing test of its own — a build error, a
'     panic outside a test — is listed as "package (package)", so a slice that
'     stops a package compiling cannot hide behind the list
' The result is compared with cmd/proveo-dev/unit-baseline.txt.
'   a failure outside the list ...... printed, exit 1
'   a listed test that passes here .. printed as a note, exit 0
' A LISTED TEST THAT PASSES DOES NOT FAIL THE GATE. The list is host-shaped:
' thirteen rows are expected to pass on Linux, so a stale-row failure would
' turn the gate red on the other host type. The note is the prompt to shrink
' the list once a row passes on both.
' A RED TEST GUARDS NOTHING. TestVarsSortByScopeThenName covers envreg.go.
' A slice that edits that file fixes line 153 first and drops the row.
' Extra arguments replace `./...`, so one package can be checked alone.
' THE GATE DOES NOT RETRY. MEASURED 2026-11-10: in one of three full runs
' TestAdbMirrorStartsWithTheSocketAddress (a shell-timing contract test) failed
' outside the list; alone it passed 6 of 6, at that tree and at the commit
' before it. A failure outside the list is rerun alone by hand. A retry inside
' the gate would also hide a test that fails only in the full run's order.
'
' Pinned by cmd/proveo-dev/baseline_test.go:
'   TestFailedTestsKeepsTopLevelFailuresAndTestlessPackages
'   TestNewFailuresSplitsAddedFromFixed
'   TestTheBaselineListIsSortedUniqueAndWellFormed
'   TestBaselineArgsDefaultToTheWholeModule

component """go test -race -json ./...""" as RUN <<app>>
component """failedTests""\ntop-level failures\nand test-less packages" as PARSE <<app>>
database """unit-baseline.txt""\n15 rows" as LIST <<db>>
component "a failure outside the list\nexit 1" as NEW <<error>>
component "a listed test that passes\na note, exit 0" as FIXED <<app>>
component """mise run ci""\nred on this host at main" as CI <<error>>

RUN ARROW_MAIN PARSE
PARSE ARROW_MAIN NEW : not in the list
PARSE ARROW_OPTIONAL FIXED : in the list, passing
LIST ARROW_MAIN NEW
LIST ARROW_OPTIONAL FIXED
CI ARROW_ERROR RUN : cannot tell old red from new

note bottom of LIST
  **Host-shaped, so it only shrinks by hand.**
  Thirteen rows are macOS tooling failures.
  A row leaves when its test passes on both
  host types, not when one host says so.
end note

note bottom of NEW
  **A build error counts.** A package that
  fails without a failing test is listed as
  its own row, so a slice cannot break a
  package and still read as green.
end note

note bottom of CI
  **Why not fix the fifteen first.** None is in
  a TUI package, and thirteen need a Linux
  host to judge. The owner chose to gate on
  "no new failure" instead.
end note
@enduml
